  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-02-13T09:39:38.631Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm not well versed in how people are able to crash your PC, ie: if it's a special shader, or too many particles. And perhaps it's impossible to implement this because they throw the entire workload at the GPU at once. But it seems to me that before a crash, the FPS always dips dramatically. So I was thinking, would it be possible to auto-enable safety settings any time the FPS drops below say, 10-15, and re-enable them after a period of time if the framerate has returned to normal? If this quick fix works, then at  least this way the only thing crashers might be able to do is hide everyone's particles and shaders for a bit.",
